+# SportsBetting_491
+
+Sports betting data collection and modeling utilities.
+
+## NBA Team and Match Data Collector
+
+The NBA collector fetches team and match/game data from ESPN's public NBA feeds
+and writes normalized JSON files that the rest of the project can consume.
+
+This is a good MVP data source because it does not require an API key. For a
+production betting product, use the same normalized output shape with a licensed
+provider such as Sportradar, SportsDataIO, or another rights-cleared source.
+
+### What it collects
+
+- NBA teams
+- NBA scheduled/live/final matches for an inclusive date range
+- Basic match status, venue, season, home/away teams, and scores
+
+### Run locally
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m sportsbetting.collectors.nba --start-date 2026-10-20 --end-date 2026-10-21
+```
+
+By default, output is written to:
+
+- `data/raw/nba/teams.json`
+- `data/raw/nba/matches.json`
+- `data/raw/nba/metadata.json`
+
+You can choose another destination:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m sportsbetting.collectors.nba \
+  --start-date 2026-10-20 \
+  --end-date 2026-10-21 \
+  --output-dir outputs/nba
+```
+
+Or print to stdout:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m sportsbetting.collectors.nba --start-date 2026-10-20 --stdout
+```
+
+### Install as a CLI
+
+```bash
+python3 -m pip install -e .
+collect-nba-data --start-date 2026-10-20 --end-date 2026-10-21
+```
+
+### Tests
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover tests
+```
